git commit -m "Fix 'name Path is not defined' in generate: import Path in output_service. My async/streaming refactor added out_path = Path(out_path_str) but output_service.py never imported Path (it only used settings.output_path, which is already a Path, via the / operator). So generate_output_artifact raised NameError, the background task caught it and set output_status=failed with 'name Path is not defined', and the poll surfaced that. Added 'from pathlib import Path'. This - not memory or the gateway timeout - is what was failing generation after the async change; with it fixed, the background flow (return immediately, poll, download when ready) should complete."
